  },
  "worker": {
    "_doc": "Fresh-context iteration agent, one queue unit per spawn. Long solver runs execute under the driver or the worker's shell - NEVER inside a background subagent (the runner's results/.run_heartbeat is the driver's dead-worker signal, and a backgrounded solve loses it). model / claude_effort apply only to Claude; codex_model / codex_reasoning_effort apply only to Codex. A blank model or effort inherits that harness's configured default. iteration_timeout_hours = the absolute cap; inactivity_timeout_min = kill a worker with no output AND no heartbeat change for this long.",
    "model": "{{WORKER_MODEL}}",
    "claude_effort": "{{WORKER_CLAUDE_EFFORT}}",
    "codex_model": "{{WORKER_CODEX_MODEL}}",
    "codex_reasoning_effort": "{{WORKER_CODEX_REASONING_EFFORT}}",
    "iteration_timeout_hours": {{ITERATION_TIMEOUT_HOURS}},
    "retries": 1,
    "inactivity_timeout_min": 30
  },
  "driver": {
    "_doc": "Supervisor-driver knobs. All code-defaulted - an older loop.json without this section keeps working. backend: auto|claude|codex|custom; new-campaign records the first launch harness here, and --backend may override it when switching. max_consecutive_failures: N operational (unit-scoped) failures in a row = systemic -> hard halt; below N the driver shelves the unit (kind=operational) and continues. planner_retries / verifier_retries: extra attempts after a planner or verifier spawn returns without its artifact (a verifier that exits ok having written no verdict is the usual case - a refuter launched in the background and abandoned - and is retried with a note naming what is missing). stream: auto|on|off - auto adds the stream-json live feed only for the default claude CLI; Codex always keeps its JSONL protocol active, while off suppresses item-level feed lines. inbox_max_chars caps the per-spawn USER-NOTES injection from results/inbox/. heartbeat_stale_min / detached_grace_min govern the post-exit wait for a detached runner that is still solving: the wait ends as soon as the heartbeat stops changing for two runner ticks (or heartbeat_stale_min if shorter), detached_grace_min being only the outer bound. permission_mode: the --permission-mode spawned workers/planners run under (default 'auto', the standard classifier: allows local file ops in project scope, reads, and killing a subprocess THIS session created by its tracked PID; cleanly denies - no prompt, verified headless - killing a process it did not create, secret writes, exfiltration, and spawning bypass agents). Set 'bypassPermissions' for a campaign that needs a soft-denied action (irreversible overwrite of a pre-existing untracked file, a cross-session kill, a force-push). Env override AUTORESEARCH_PERMISSION_MODE; only applied to the default claude CLI.",
    "backend": "{{AGENT_BACKEND}}",
    "max_consecutive_failures": 3,
    "planner_retries": 1,
    "verifier_retries": 1,
    "stream": "auto",
    "permission_mode": "auto",
    "inbox_max_chars": 20000,
    "feed_line_chars": 160,
    "heartbeat_stale_min": 5,
    "detached_grace_min": 60
  },
  "verify": {
    "_doc": "How much verification this campaign buys, and of what kind - ONE choice, preset: minimal | light | moderate | intensive (the standardized descriptions are the physkit plugin's docs/reference/verification-presets.md; the runner prints the resolved table at preflight and stamps it into every results/checks_<NN>.json). light (the default): cheap invariants every unit, the authored checks at setup, an independent fresh-context review before each promotion, the claim audit at the end. moderate: as light, plus the authored checks re-run whenever the code they cover changes, and an independent check before each promotion that RE-EXECUTES the unit when it is cheap and reproducible. intensive: every check and an independent check every unit (batched per block), a different-model refuter where an adapter is configured, blinded from the narrative, a panel claim audit. minimal: the floor and cheap invariants only, no independent check, every claim exported 'unverified' - reserved until the promotion guard can stamp that word. Whatever the preset: the runner floor (scorer selftest, the checks artifact, ledger and epoch gates) always runs; every result carries the preset it ran under; re-execution depth is decided per unit from its MEASURED solve time (within a quarter of worker.iteration_timeout_hours) and campaign.reproducible, recorded under verification.re_execution; derived numbers are ALWAYS recomputed from raw artifacts. Changing the preset mid-campaign is legitimate and logged by the driver. A file without preset is read as the previous kit read campaign.verification (per-block | promotion-only). strategy: auto preserves the nested verifier for Claude/custom and uses one fresh driver-direct refuter turn for Codex; legacy-nested forces the nested path; driver-direct is Codex-only. A full_reproduction_threshold_s left by an older scaffold is honoured as an additional cap.",
    "preset": "{{VERIFICATION_PRESET}}",
    "strategy": "auto"
  }
}
